line 16, 17, 29 type: by-design spec §1.6 `&&` keeps `number` and `boolean` whole in its falsy part, where tsc narrows to `0` or `false`
line 18 type: bug SUB-1196 (guard on a getter read) a guard doesn't narrow a later read of a getter, since each read may return a different value; also by-design spec §1.6 `&&` keeps `number` and `boolean` whole in its falsy part, where tsc narrows to `0` or `false`
